            "why": "Each glyph in a sigil reads as what it does, so a reader can tell the mark that closes a sigil from the verb it closes. The `~` marker every sigil opens with announces that the dialect speaks here, and reads with the verb as the dialect's keyword; the `/` close mark carries structure and reads quiet, as punctuation. The verb names an act and reads as a keyword of the dialect."
